    "id": "why",
    "title": "The missing voltage",
    "labels": [
      "Reliability",
      "Stimulation",
      "Voltage"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Modern systems can run remarkably well without anyone feeling inspired.",
      "This essay asks why a civilization so rich in possibility struggles to commit.",
      "Its answer is enthusiasm: voluntary energy toward a future you can help shape.",
      "Stimulation keeps nudging attention; voltage is the sense that effort moves something worthwhile."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "calm recognition of a working world rises to the tension of an unanswered question, released by a precise definition",
